  "summary": "When Tim Costello was in year 9, he asked his teacher if poverty was something natural and unchangeable, like the sun rising or the tide going out. He learned that poverty is not natural, but caused by the choices people make. This idea has guided his life. Now 69 years old, Tim Costello has spent more than 30 years working to fight poverty in Australia. He has traveled around the world to places affected by war and disasters, served as mayor of St Kilda, written books, and been honored as a national treasure. People sometimes mix him up with his brother, Peter Costello, who was a government treasurer. Before meeting Tim, some people ask if he is the one involved with the Liberal party or the church. Tim is well-known as a Baptist church leader and as the CEO of World Vision, a charity he led for 13 years."
